<spell-page "root theming" notebook>
	<header level="1">
		Root
		<header>A root loads the components inside it on demand, sets their theme, size, icons and emoji, and shows
              them once they're ready.</>
	</>
	<section>
		<toolbar class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#defaults">Defaults</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  no tokens of its own;  what it sets for what's inside. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			A root has no look of its own, so no `--ui-root-*` tokens. It themes what's INSIDE it:

			- `theme="light"` / `"dark"` sets the colour scheme of everything inside (`:state(light)` / `:state(dark)`).
			- `size` scales the components inside, `mini` ... `massive` (not plain text, nor a bare `<ui-icon>`, which follows its text).
			- Any `--ui-*` token set on the root inherits into every element inside, as on any ancestor.
			- Style the loading look with `::part(loading)` (the loader) and `::part(skeleton)` (the placeholders' box), and
			  a box's scroller with `::part(scroller)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-root.dashboard {
			  --ui-primary: var(--ui-teal);
			}
			ui-root.dashboard::part(skeleton) {
			  padding: 1em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-root" playground>
				<ui-root>
					<ui-segment>
						<ui-header>Report</>
						<ui-text paragraph>Every component inside was loaded by the root, on demand.</>
						<ui-button color="primary">Save</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Defaults">
		<markdown>
			A root gives the widgets inside it attribute values they don't set themselves:  every button a pill, every
			segment raised.  A widget's own attribute still wins.

			An app says its defaults in Spell, in a `<ui-defaults>` block of sample tags, one per widget, at a file's top:

			```spell
			<ui-defaults>
			  <ui-button appearance="pill"/>
			  <ui-segment appearance="raised"/>
			</ui-defaults>
			```

			- Any attribute but what a widget shows (`label`, `value`, `text`).  A widget, attribute or value Spell UI
			  doesn't have is an error naming what it takes.
			- A Spanish file writes the same block in Spell UI's Spanish words:  `<es-boton apariencia="píldora"/>`.
			- Another project's defaults:  `<ui-defaults source="@spell/library/theme/ui-defaults.spell"/>`, with that
			  project in your project file's imports.
			- The Inspector says "From ui-defaults" on a value that came from them, naming the file.

			On a page, the root's `defaults` takes the same, tag by tag, as JSON or as a property:

			```html
			<ui-root defaults='{"ui-button": {"appearance": "pill"}}'>
			  <ui-button color="primary">Save</ui-button>
			  <ui-button appearance="basic">Cancel</ui-button>
			</ui-root>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Root is ours, not Fomantic's, and draws nothing itself, so no theme restyles it. The site-wide theme (the picker in
			the header) applies to everything inside a root.
		</>
	</>
</spell-page>
